### Phase 2 — strategist becomes optional (DONE, commit `3165f64`)

The pipeline gains a major shape: synthesize is no longer the default
path. Most modules are navigation stubs.

- Stages 2 (Research) and 3 (Synthesize) are now conditional, gated on
  the spec-writer's two new return signals: **Research needed (yes/no)**
  and **Strategy needed (yes/no)**. Default both to NO.
- New routing decision table after Stage 1 maps signals to next stage.
- Stage 4 (Plan) splits into **Shape A** (synthesize ran — body sections
  filled, `brief.aide` exists) and **Shape B** (synthesize skipped —
  frontmatter-only spec; orchestrator passes user implementation
  context to architect verbatim).
- Resume Protocol updated: frontmatter-only spec without `plan.aide`
  defaults to Plan, asks user before routing to Synthesize.
- "just plan it" recognized as explicit intent that skips synthesize.
- `aide-spec.md` "Body sections (required)" → "Body sections
  (conditional)". When present, all five appear together (no partial
  bodies). Body sections persist when filled, like frontmatter.
- `aide-template.md` instructs writers to delete the entire body block
  when synthesize will not run.
- Spec-writer outcome caps fixed at 3-6 (matches aide-spec.md).
- Strategist all-or-nothing rule: if invoked, fill all five sections;
  escalate to research rather than producing a thin body. Context cap
  150 → 250 words, Strategy 5 → 7 decisions to match aide-spec.md.
- Architect Shape A vs Shape B branching. Reads `brief.aide` only if
  it exists. Creates `brief.aide` in Shape B only when commitments
  surface; most simple Shape-B modules don't need one.

