## Anti-regression invariants from prior brain-config rework (still current)

These describe the CURRENT shape of the brain layer. Slimmer leaf specs
written in any future sweep must accurately reflect them, not contradict
them. Numbering preserved from the prior handoff so plan/PR references
remain stable.

1. **`brain.aide` lives at `.aide/config/brain.aide`.** The
   `.aide/config/` directory is user-owned: scaffolded once at
   `aide_init` if absent, never overwritten by `aide_init` or
   `aide_upgrade` afterward. Path itself is the ownership signal.

2. **Default scaffolded launcher is `@bitbonsai/mcpvault`.** The
   bundled `obsidianBrainAideTemplate()` helper takes no `brainPath`
   parameter and emits YAML null at `args[3]` (the path slot for the
   bundled Obsidian default).

3. **`brain.aide` frontmatter schema = exactly two top-level fields:**
   `name` (label, never branched on) and `mcpServerConfig`
   (`command` + `args`, written verbatim into `.mcp.json` under
   `mcpServers["brain"]` by `npx @aidemd-mcp/server@latest sync`).

4. **`brain.aide` body schema = exactly six marker-bounded sections,
   fixed order:** orientation, config, playbook-index, study-playbook,
   update-playbook, research-index. Markers are paired
   `<!-- aide-X-start -->` / `<!-- aide-X-end -->`, lowercase,
   case-sensitive.

5. **Two structural categories of body section:**
   - **Live (read by `aide_brain` at runtime):** `orientation`,
     `config`.
   - **Install-time seeds:** `playbookIndex` →
     `coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md`, `studyPlaybook` →
     `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md`, `updatePlaybook` →
     `coding-playbook/update-playbook.md`, `researchIndex` →
     `research/research.md`.
   - Cross-section reads across this boundary are forbidden.

6. **`aide_brain({ kind?: "orientation" | "config" })`** — closed
   two-value vocabulary, default `"orientation"`, response shape
   `{ status, instructions }` only.

7. **`parseBrainAide` ok-variant is FLATTENED.** `name` and
   `mcpServerConfig` are siblings of the six body fields.
   `mcpServerConfig.args` is typed `(string | null)[]`.

8. **Entry-point artifact bytes flow from `brain.aide` body sections,
   never from inline TypeScript constants.** Seed bytes live in the
   bundled template's body sections.

9. **Framework's brain contract = exactly four required entry-point
   artifacts:** the three coding-playbook files plus the research
   index. **Seeded by the integration's `config` body section prose
   at first `/aide:brain config`**, not by `provisionBrain`.

10. **Boot reporter brain status states = four:** `ok`,
    `no-brain-aide`, `no-mcp-entry`, `mcp-drift`. Closed vocabulary.
    Null-armed args collapse semantically into `no-mcp-entry`.

11. **`provisionBrain` accepts NO `brainPath` parameter** at any layer.
    No `brainPath` on the orchestrator signature, on any per-step
    builder, or on the bundled template helper.

12. **`cli/init` is brain-agnostic on the cold-start path.** Writes
    ZERO brain surfaces at install: no `.mcp.json` brain entry, no
    `provisionBrain` MCP-entry-plan call, no brain root directory
    creation, no backend-specific user prompts. Accepts only
    `--brain <integration>` (default `obsidian`) and writes the
    bundled template with YAML null at unwired slots. Brain wiring
    is delegated to `/aide:brain config` on first `/aide` run.

13. **Removed `brain.aide` frontmatter fields** (parser actively
    rejects): `connector`, `rootPath`, `entryFile`, `tools`.

14. **No code path branches on `name`.** It's a label.

15. **No introspection of `mcpServerConfig.args` for any purpose.** No
    `PATH_SLOT_INDEX` constant, no `args[N]` switch, no matcher
    recognizing token-shaped strings, no `argSlots` frontmatter field,
    no `resolveBrainRoot`-style helper.

16. **`${...}` interpolation of frontmatter values into
    `mcpServerConfig.args`** is supported for advanced users; runs
    ONLY at install/sync time, NEVER against any of the six body
    sections.

17. **The MCP server NEVER silently rewrites `.mcp.json`.** Sync is
    the only mutation surface for `mcpServers.brain`.

18. **Storage-agnostic vocabulary across every package surface.**
    Forbidden tokens — `vault`, `obsidian`, `note` (as a synonym for
    "file"), `wikilink`, `hub note`, `hub` — must not appear in
    user-facing prose, code identifiers, comments, or string
    constants. Three carve-outs: the `obsidianBrainAideTemplate`
    helper folder/function name; the `.obsidian` directory heuristic
    in `brainRootExists`; the body-section bytes of the bundled
    `obsidianBrainAideTemplate` (those bytes are user-owned).

19. **`mcpServerConfig.args` is typed `(string | null)[]`.** Null at
    any index is the explicit, structural, unwired-slot signal. NO
    literal-string sentinel anywhere.

20. **`provisionBrain` is a TWO-step pipeline:** brain.aide scaffold +
    MCP entry plan only. The four entry-point artifacts are seeded by
    the integration's `config` body section prose at `/aide:brain
    config`, NOT by `provisionBrain`.

21. **`buildBrainState` maps null entries in `mcpServerConfig.args`
    to `no-mcp-entry`** structurally (JS `=== null` against parsed
    YAML). Null-args check runs BEFORE the byte-for-byte drift
    comparison.

22. **`cli/sync` refuses null-bearing args at the boundary.** Exits
    non-zero, names the offending index(es), routes user to
    `/aide:brain config`. Sync is precondition-not-transformation.

23. **`/aide:brain config` Mode 2** calls `aide_init({ category:
    "brain" })` UNCONDITIONALLY at the top of every invocation —
    enables missing-`brain.aide` recovery.

24. **Per-integration ownership of arg-index slot semantics.** Slot
    meanings live EXCLUSIVELY in the integration's `config` body
    section. Shipped code never hardcodes a slot index, never has a
    registry of slot meanings, never has a per-index validation
    table.

25. **Legacy `mcpServers.obsidian` migration is dropped entirely.**
    No code path reads, writes, removes, or detects the legacy key.

26. **Strict-failure migration for body-schema and frontmatter shape
    changes.** Pre-rework files fail closed as `malformed-body` /
    `malformed-frontmatter`. No auto-migration, no transitional read
    path.

27. **Shipped pipeline command surfaces are thin routers/pointers.**

28. **`.claude/` is never pipelined.** Direct edits only. Per-command
    `.aide` specs are an anti-pattern. `.aide/docs/`,
    `.aide/intent.aide`, and `.aide/config/brain.aide` ARE
    pipeline-appropriate when their updates ride alongside a code
    amendment.

