## Where the cycle paused

All three phases are now landed locally:

- `feat/lean-pipeline-recovery` (Phase 1 + 2) — pushed; PR opens at
  https://github.com/aidemd-mcp/server/pull/new/feat/lean-pipeline-recovery
- `feat/leaf-stub-sweep` (Phase 3) — local only; not yet pushed.

The `.mcp.json` in this repo is set to dev form
(`node ./dist/index.js`). During this cycle a stale `dist/` with
unresolved `@/tools` aliases broke the aide MCP server entry; fixed by
running the full `npm run build` chain (which includes `tsc-alias`).
Future agents picking up cold should run `npm run build` if the aide
MCP fails to register — `npm run dev` (just `tsc --watch`) skips the
alias rewrite step and produces the same failure.

Decision points awaiting the user:

1. **Push and merge order.** Push `feat/leaf-stub-sweep` and open a
   second PR? Merge `lean-pipeline-recovery` first, then rebase the
   sweep, or land them as independent PRs against `main`?
2. **Maintainer agent design.** Still deferred. Now is the right time
   to design and ship — the methodology has earned it (49 orphaned
   ephemerals had to be hand-deleted at the start of the sweep
   because no maintainer existed to do it post-QA).
3. **Retro promotion to brain.** `process/retro/` has not yet received
   the retro from this multi-cycle effort. Should land before
   `session.aide` is eventually deleted.

